\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (Top) Coarse-grained representation of the charged CPPM variants: $P^{0}_{0}$, $P^{1}_{8}$ and $P^{2}_{8}$ along with the net charge, the magnitude of the dipole moment $\mu $ and the Frobenius norm of the traceless quadrupole tensor $\Theta $. Color coding: gray = center particle, red = positive surface group, blue = negative surface group. (Bottom) Surface charge density mapped onto the unit sphere via the Mollweide equal-area projection where the charges are smeared with a spherical smoothing kernel. All projections share a common color scale anchored to the model with the widest density range. White squares ($\square $) indicate the two poles of the dipole moment. White triangles ($\vartriangle $/$\triangledown $) indicate the two antipodal poles of the prolate axis of quadrupole tensor, and black triangles ($\blacktriangle $/$\blacktriangledown $) the oblate axis. Marker size scales qualitatively with the magnitude of the corresponding moment.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cppms}{{1}{5}}
