\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Radial distribution functions $g(r)$ at the best-fit Debye screening length $\kappa ^{-1}_*$ for the three charged CPPM variants: (a)\nobreakspace  {}$P^{0}_{0}$ ($\kappa ^{-1}_* = \qty {37.9}{\angstrom }$, dotted), (b)\nobreakspace  {}$P^{1}_{8}$ ($\kappa ^{-1}_* = \qty {12.5}{\angstrom }$, dashed), and (c)\nobreakspace  {}$P^{2}_{8}$ ($\kappa ^{-1}_* = \qty {16.7}{\angstrom }$, solid). Upper sub-panel: implicit-ion $g(r)$ at $\kappa ^{-1}_*$ (colored lines); implicit-ion $g(r)$ at the screening length $\kappa ^{-1}_\mathrm  {th} = \qty {9.61}{\angstrom }$ predicted from the explicit-ion ionic strength (gray); and the explicit-ion reference (black lines). Shaded bands indicate the mean $\pm $ SEM across replicas. Lower sub-panel: residuals $\Delta g(r) = g_\mathrm  {imp}(r) - g_\mathrm  {exp}(r)$ with propagated uncertainty; the horizontal gray dashed line marks zero.}}{14}{}\protected@file@percent }
